e2950ff5 (3149 1792876136232 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f338") (src . "test: cli1's three barrier releases end, by one bounded write\n\ncli1.sc released a holder parked at a barrier (ffi.sc barrier!) in two\nshapes that could hang the fixture to the runner's alarm: P4 started a\ndecoy `head -c 1` reader so that its bounded write had somewhere to go,\nand that reader could take the byte in the window between the holder's\ntrace line and its open, leaving the holder waiting for a writer that\nnever came; two-writers and P9 wrote with no bound at all, so a holder\nthat never reached its open held the shell for good.\n\n- One procedure, release-text (gate pid-var bound): the write itself is\n  the handshake (an open for writing blocks until the holder opens), done\n  by one foreground perl under its own alarm, so nothing holds a pid to\n  signal later; on expiry the holder is killed too, so the caller's final\n  `wait` returns; `released` says whether the write completed. Used at\n  the three sites, each echoing RELEASED and gaining one row that wants\n  yes; the pinned rows are unchanged.\n- Two CONTROLs: a stub holder that writes its barrier line and never\n  opens the gate (bound 2 s: reads no, ends under 10 s, the stub dead,\n  no writer left behind, the gate drained afterwards) and one that opens\n  at once (reads yes inside the bound). On the previous text both shapes\n  hang (measured under a 60 s alarm).\n- test/rows-baseline.txt: cli1 105 131.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 471))))
